Now the escapeSequence rewrite. Let's replace the entire function from `async escapeSequence()` to before `escapeFailed()`. This is a big replacement. We'll write the new function.

Need to ensure the camera and player position. The standoff leaves Tim at (8.2,0,-16.4) inside fuel room. We'll reset to that. The locker is pushed to the door. Start timer 30s. Set state active, escapePhase 'jack', show jack marker. Mace at door. Captions. No auto-run.

Let's write:

```
async escapeSequence() {
  if (this.disposed) return;
  this.state='sequence';
  this.escapeAttempts++;
  this.dead=false;
  ...
  if (this.escapeAttempts>1) { reset... }
  this.interior.resetEscape();
  this.interior.resetJack();
  this.hasJack=false;
  this.escapePhase='jack';
  this.escape={time:30, active:true};
  showEscapeTimer(true); update...
  this.tim.group.position.set(8.2,0,-16.4); rotation 0; setCrouch(0); poseLock=false;
  this.mace... position (8.4,0,-11.9) ...
  this.camera...
  this.interior.closeKeypadDoor(); blockFuelDoor(); 
  // Mace slams locker
  ...
  this.callbacks.onObjective?.('TAKE THE SCISSOR JACK','The work table. Move.');
  this.interior.showJackMarker(true);
  this.state='active';
  audio.setMood('encounter');
  this.caption('MACE','Thirty seconds, kid. Thirty!',2.8);
  this.caption('', 'The locker hit the frame. The fuel door buckled — but it held.', 3.0);
  this.addShake(0.1);
}
```

Wait, `interior.closeKeypadDoor()` and `blockFuelDoor()` immediately, plus locker animation. We can animate the locker from its original position to the door in a tween, but state should be active after. Since escapeSequence is async, we can do a short await then set active. But we want the player control quickly. Do:
```
this.interior.closeKeypadDoor();
const locker = this.interior.locker;
const lFrom = locker.position.clone();
const lTo = new THREE.Vector3(7.6,0,-13.2);
this.state='sequence';
await this.tween(0.7, u=>{ locker.position.lerpVectors(...); ... camera ...});
this.interior.blockFuelDoor();
this.state='active';
...
```
But during this sequence, the timer is active; updateEscapeTimer runs even in sequence. Fine.
Then set objective and captions. But `await this.wait` would block the player control. Avoid long waits. Use captions without awaits.

Need `this.escapePhase` to persist. On failure, `escapeFailed` resets.

`useJackOnDoor()`:
```
